course: dictionary
lesson: 8128
title: Sorry, and really meaning it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Repentant is an adjective, a describing word. It means you feel sorry for something wrong you have done, and you want to put it right. It is about feeling sorry and wanting to change, not just saying sorry.
explain: Context helps you check. «You're so eloquent, dear Badger … I find that I'm not a bit sorry or repentant really.» The speaker says he is not sorry, so he does not feel repentant. Swap in the meaning: "I am not a bit sorry for what I did, and I do not want to change" fits the sentence.
explain: In stories, Toad can be repentant for a while, then go back to being boastful again. A feeling of sorrow can fade. Look for clues like "for a while" or "then" to see whether the sorry feeling lasts.
fact: Repentant means feeling sorry for something wrong you have done and wanting to change.
fact: Repentant is an adjective, so it describes a person: a repentant thief is a thief who is truly sorry.
fact: Sorry and repentant are close, but repentant goes further, because you also want to change what you do.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is repentant for a while, then becomes boastful again.
fact: In church, repentant means sorry for sins; Christians believe God forgives the repentant.
exercise: «I find that I'm not a bit sorry or repentant really.» What does repentant mean? | Wanting to show off | Happy to win a prize | Very tired after a long day | *Feeling sorry for something wrong and wanting to change
exercise: The repentant thief on the cross was sorry for his wrong. What does repentant show about the thief? | *He was truly sorry for what he had done | He was proud of his crimes | He was lost on the road | He had never done anything wrong
exercise: Toad says he is «not a bit sorry». What does «not a bit» show? | He is very sorry | He is a little bit sorry | *He is not sorry at all | He is unsure what to feel
test: In the story, Toad is repentant for a while, then boastful again. What happens to his sorry feeling? | He becomes a thief | *It does not last, and he goes back to boasting | They stay the same forever | He is always repentant
test: What does repentant mean in church? | Angry at God | *Sorry for sins, and believing God forgives the repentant | Happy and proud | Lost in the woods
exam: Which sentence uses repentant correctly? | The repentant bus was late again this morning. | The repentant sun shone brightly over the hills. | *The repentant child said sorry and promised to help tidy up. | The repentant tree was very tall and green.
